The train drove quickly through the landscape.
I sat quietly in my seat.
I had a really good window seat.
After a little while, we finally reached the coast.
The train drove out onto a very long bridge over the sea.
Suddenly there was only water all around us.
The bridge lay high above the water.
I looked out of the large window.
The water below us was very blue.
I admired the beautiful, open view.
Far below, I saw some small ships.
They almost looked like toys.
The sky was light blue and completely without clouds.
It was almost like flying over the sea.
I took my camera out of my bag.
I took a couple of pictures of the small ships.
I had never seen anything like it.
Afterwards, I put my camera away and just enjoyed the journey.
